      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose for adults.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** 6,400 mg/day is twice the 3,200 mg/day ceiling. Even that ceiling is for supervised use, and 1,200 mg/day is typical for OTC use.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The risk is high even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, as is sometimes used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and add the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
